1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:06,958
Demo: running automated Playwright tests from the browser, without VS Code

2
00:00:06,958 --> 00:00:12,169
This is the Test Runner. It opens automatically when "Start Test Runner" is double-clicked.

3
00:00:12,169 --> 00:00:15,675
Step 1: choose a test suite: Smoke, Sanity, Regression or Broken links.

4
00:00:15,675 --> 00:00:19,870
Regression runs all 17 tests, including the broken link check.

5
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:24,569
Step 2 (optional): type the email ID(s) that should receive the report.

6
00:00:24,569 --> 00:00:29,269
By default the report is emailed only if a Critical bug is found.

7
00:00:29,269 --> 00:00:35,239
Headed mode shows a real browser running the tests. For this recording it is switched off.

8
00:00:35,239 --> 00:00:39,268
Step 3: press Run tests. Results arrive live, test by test.

9
00:00:39,268 --> 00:00:45,250
The progress bar fills in green for passed and red for failed tests.

10
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:51,012
Finished: 11 of 17 tests failed. These are the bugs planted on purpose in the demo shop.

11
00:00:51,012 --> 00:00:56,227
The full report opens in the same UI. The run name starts with the date and time.

12
00:00:56,227 --> 00:01:00,844
Pass rate and totals at a glance.

13
00:01:00,844 --> 00:01:08,197
Results by module, and bug severity predicted by the Machine Learning model. Critical bugs are highlighted.

14
00:01:08,197 --> 00:01:13,928
Click a failed test to see its error message and the screenshot taken at the moment of failure.

15
00:01:13,928 --> 00:01:19,226
Screenshots open full size: the payment gateway crashed with a 500 error.

16
00:01:19,226 --> 00:01:28,304
Every failed test has its own Re-run button. It runs only that one test again.

17
00:01:28,304 --> 00:01:32,319
Only the selected test ran again, and the bug is confirmed.

18
00:01:32,319 --> 00:01:36,833
Run History keeps every run, grouped by day and named with its date first.

19
00:01:36,833 --> 00:01:42,596
Every failure is logged as a bug automatically: no manual bug reporting.

20
00:01:42,596 --> 00:01:47,809
Each bug has its error, screenshot, ML severity with confidence, and status history.

21
00:01:47,809 --> 00:01:52,324
A tester moves the bug from Open to In Progress to Resolved; every change is recorded.

22
00:01:52,324 --> 00:01:56,836
Flaky tests, which pass and fail at random, are detected across runs.

23
00:01:56,836 --> 00:02:01,850
Analytics: open bugs, Critical bugs, bugs per module, severity and the 14-day trend.

24
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:12,346
The website under test is ShopEase, a demo shop with bugs planted on purpose.

25
00:02:12,346 --> 00:02:22,228
Searching in capitals finds nothing: a Major bug found by the tests.

26
00:02:22,228 --> 00:02:27,233
Placing an order fails with a server error: a Critical bug, which also triggers the email alert.

27
00:02:27,233 --> 00:02:33,237
To try it: install Node.js, then double-click "Start Test Runner" in the project folder.
